Overview 
 We are looking for an experienced IT Infrastructure Integrator to join our engineering team. In this role, you will contribute to the design, implementation, and integration of IT infrastructures supporting air traffic management and other aviation-related systems. 
 You will work closely with project managers, technical teams, and end clients to ensure systems are deployed according to strict performance, security, and regulatory requirements. 
 Responsa ibilities 
 Contribute to the design and deployment of secure, scalable IT infrastructure solutions; Install, configure, and maintain Linux-based servers and virtualization platforms (KVM, Proxmox); 
 Automate deployment and operational processes using tools such as Ansible, Shell scripting, and PowerShell; 
 Manage and maintain networking components (switching, routing, VPNs, firewalls); 
 Ensure infrastructure compliance with security, availability, and performance standards; 
 Produce and maintain high-quality technical documentation in line with industry regulations; 
 Support on-site installations and integration activities at customer locations; 
 Participate in technical meetings with clients and internal stakeholders; 
 Provide post-deployment support and produce intervention and service reports. 
 Requirements 
 Significant experience (minimum 5 years) in a similar role, ideally in a civil aviation-related environment; 
 Strong expertise in: Linux server administration, Virtualization technologies (KVM, Proxmox), Networking fundamentals and security, Infrastructure automation tools; 
 Excellent technical documentation skills; 
 Fluent English (spoken and written); 
 Availability to travel internationally for on-site project activities. Travel intensity may vary depending on project phase and can reach up to 50% during deployment periods; 
 Strong communication and teamwork skills; 
 Ability to work independently and solve complex technical issues; 
 Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field. 
 Nice to have 
 Experience working in regulated or mission-critical environments (aviation, transport, energy, telecom) is a strong advantage; 
 What We Offer 
 Opportunities to grow through involvement in complex international projects; 
 A collaborative environment with knowledge-sharing initiatives and technical communities; 
 Meal vouchers as part of your monthly benefits; Private medical insurance, supporting your health and wellbeing; 
 25 days of annual paid leave under a full-time employment contract; 
 Flexible working arrangements, aligned with project requirements and client environments; 
 Access to technical training programs and professional development resources. 
 Ready to embed yourself in the future? Let’s partner with us to power what’s next! 
 *Please note that only suitable candidates will be contacted and that by applying to this role you are being informed about your personal data being processed by Avel Technologies.
